course: dictionary
lesson: 2871
title: Donation: giving to help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A donation is something you give to help someone else, and you are not paid for it. It can be money, food, clothes or toys. Read the words around it: «Charities use donations to buy food, medicine and blankets.» The clues are charities, buy food, medicine and blankets, so donations must be gifts that help people who need them.
explain: Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence. «Saying no to organ donation is a personal choice that is respected.» The clues are personal choice and respected, so donation is a decision to give something, here an organ, to help another person. Try swapping in the word gift. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Some phrases use donation together. You can make a donation, you can put coins in a donation box, and a blood donation means giving some of your blood. When you learn a phrase, you learn how the word is used in real life, which helps you read and write it well.
fact: A donation is something given to help others, without payment.
fact: Donations can be money, food, clothes, toys or blood.
fact: A blood donation means giving some of your blood to help someone else.
fact: Organ donation is a personal choice, and people's choices about it are respected.
fact: Most Christian churches support organ donation as an act of love.
exercise: «Charities use donations to buy food, medicine and blankets.» What is a donation? | *Something given to help others, without payment | A fast car | A kind of school lunch | A toy shop receipt
exercise: Our school is holding a food donation day. What are pupils asked to bring? | Tickets for the cinema | Homework books | *Tins of food to give to the food bank | Shoes for their own feet
exercise: «Saying no to organ donation is a personal choice that is respected.» What does this sentence tell you? | Donations are always money | Organs are sold in shops | *People can choose whether to give an organ, and their choice is respected | Everyone must give an organ
test: Which of these is a donation? | A ticket you buy for a football match | *Clothes you give to a charity shop for others | A bill you must pay | A loan from the bank
test: «Healthy adults can give about half a litre at a blood donation to help people after accidents.» What is a blood donation? | Counting how much blood you have | *Giving some of your blood to help someone else | Taking blood from a sick person | Buying blood from a hospital
exam: Which phrase means giving money or goods to help others? | Sports day | *Make a donation | Blood test | Lost property
